    dict(key='18-act-5-figure', kind='figure', title='History is kept in full, for thirty days',
         body='cost',
         narration='Fifth demo: how long to keep history, and what it costs. [[slnc 400]] At the top, the lifecycle rule. [[slnc 300]] An old version is removed thirty days after it is replaced. [[slnc 600]] Now the cost, worked out. [[slnc 300]] An orders file of two megabytes, overwritten every hour. [[slnc 300]] Twenty four versions a day, times thirty days, is seven hundred and twenty old versions. [[slnc 600]] Every version is stored in full. [[slnc 300]] Seven hundred and twenty times two megabytes is one thousand four hundred and forty megabytes. [[slnc 300]] For one two megabyte file. [[slnc 600]] Each block on the bar is one day: forty eight megabytes. [[slnc 300]] After thirty days, the oldest block goes. [[slnc 300]] The rule keeps the history bounded, but not free.'),
