    dict(key='31-outro', kind='outro', title='Thanks for Watching',
         body=['Full source, notes, diagrams and an animated walkthrough', 'are in the repository. Try a GOVERNANCE lock', 'with a ten second retention.'],
         narration="That's backups with an object store. [[slnc 400]] If you remember one sentence, make it this one. [[slnc 300]] A backup is safe when the old data is kept, when it cannot be deleted before a date, and when the job that writes it can do nothing but add. [[slnc 500]] The full source code, written notes, diagrams, and an animated walkthrough are all in the repository. [[slnc 300]] It runs on your own machine, with Docker and a Java development kit. [[slnc 500]] Here is one exercise to try. [[slnc 300]] Make a governance lock with a ten second retention, and watch it expire. [[slnc 500]] If you found this useful, a like really helps other people discover it. [[slnc 300]] Kindly subscribe to the channel. [[slnc 300]] It helps the channel grow and bring you more content. [[slnc 400]] Thanks for watching!"),
